            "anchor": "data-movement-and-conversion-instructions-mov",
            "startLine": 15047,
            "endLine": 15052,
            "page": 270
          },
          "quotation": "Although only predicate and bit-size types are required, we include the arithmetic types for the programmer’s convenience: their use enhances program readability and allows additional type checking.\nWhen moving address of a kernel or a device function, only .u32 or .u64 instruction types are allowed. However, if a signed type is used, it is not treated as a compilation error. The compiler issues a warning in this case."
